{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-q-dilog-three-contexts","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:q-dilog-three-contexts","kind":"remark","title":"$\\mathrm{Li}_2^q$ in $\\mathbb{F}_p$, $\\mathbb{Q}_p$, $\\mathbb{C}_p$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-dilogarithm"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-dilogarithm","tags":["hopf-algebra","dilogarithm","p-adic","finite-field","q-series"],"text":"q-dilog-three-contexts.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:q-dilog-three-contexts\"></a><p>The extra denominator <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> forces tighter convergence constraints. Over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{F}_p</code>, the series truncates to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{Li}_2^{q,(p)}(x) = \\sum_{n=1}^{p-1} x^n / (n [n]_q)</code>. Over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}_p</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}_p</code>, it converges within <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v_p(x) > 1/(p-1)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-dilog-three-contexts.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.23.5"}
